# Rocci in five minutes

**Prerequisites:** [Install Rocci](/docs/start/install/).
**You will build:** nothing new. You will lower and preview `Hello` from the
checked-in styling example.
**Time:** about five minutes after the CLI is built.
**Verify:** the preview shows **Hello, Ada**.
**Next:** [Build your first component](/docs/tutorials/first-component/).

This page is evaluative. It is not the full tutorial.

## 1. Lower the module

From the repository root:

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- build \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
```

Stdout is ordinary Roc. Find `hello = |{ name }|`. The PascalCase component
`Hello` became a camelCase function. `@css` became scoped CSS metadata.
Rocci did not type-check the module; Roc will, when you run or view it.

## 2. Preview one component

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- view \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci \
  --component Hello --arg name=Ada
```

Rocci compiles the module, starts a local HTTP server, prints the URL, and
opens the native preview window. Add `--no-window` and open the URL yourself
if you do not want the webview.

**Verify:** a greeting that reads **Hello, Ada**. The fixture `helloTest`
also supplies `{ name: "Ada" }` when you omit `--arg`.

## 3. One boundary

| Authored | Generated |
| --- | --- |
| `@component Hello = \|{ name ?? "Roc" }\|` | `hello = \|{ name }\|` plus a default at call sites |
| `<p class="greeting">` | `Html.element("p", [Html.attribute("class", "greeting")], …)` |
| `{name}` | `Html.text(name)` — must be `Str` |

`??` defaults are a Rocci convenience. The current Roc nightly rejects `??`
in patterns, so lowering strips them. That status is **experimental**.

## If it failed

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `roc` not found | Toolchain | [Install](/docs/start/install/) |
| Unknown component | Name mismatch | Use `Hello` or `hello` |
| No window | Webview / display | Rerun with `--no-window` and open the printed URL |

Complete source: [Styling](/examples/styling/) ·
[Styling.rocci](/examples/styling/source/Styling-rocci/).

Next: [Build your first component](/docs/tutorials/first-component/) to add
